ese treats?\" The little pig was intrigued. He was always a sucker for good dessert. Even if Anders was a wolf, it was a nice gesture for him to bring desserts. So the little wolf agreed to meet Anders and share the treats, though the little pig insisted that they meet outside of the house. \"We can meet in my backyard,\" the little pig said. He was going to take every precaution with this wolf. Anders relented. He could make friends with the pig regardless of the location, even if the little pig wasn't being totally hospitable. So they met in the backyard. The little pig was surprised to see that the wolf had also brought a whole picnic basket full of delicacies, including cheese sandwiches, cold fried chicken, potato salad, egg salad, potato chips, and chocolate cake. Not only that, but the basket also had a bottle of wine and a bottle of champagne. \"Wow,\" the little pig said. \"You really went all out.\" The two animals snacked and wined and dined on the food that Anders had brought. The little pig was very impressed. He realized that Anders was actually a very good conversation partner. He was well-read and had a lot of interesting things to say.",
